<<~ ahu slot=`#/glass-lane-ii-out-2026-11-11`>>

! Glass lane II — out (Glass-Wright II: Lares (Tasked Spirit), 2026-11-11)

Branch `feature/green-jello-dinosaur-5--glass2`, cut at 407f3251d and pushed. Two commits:
* `18c05e779 lar:///floor.reaches.wiki/oracle-replay` — the floor's rows now land in every island's engine.
* `a8f6058d0 lar:///pane.holds.viewport/glass-sheet` — the mirror's host acts as the engine's viewport; the pane's ground uses the palette colour; weld M2 updated to match.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/the-three-defects-read`>>

!! The three defects, read

# ''The sidebar escaped the pane.'' Confirmed: at 1400×900 the sidebar painted at (1050, 0), 350×900, on the window.
#* Cure: `packages/lararium-tw5/src/glass-sheet.ts` (`shadowSheet`, `GLASS_FRAME_SHEET`), called by `glass-camera.ts` on every sheet render.
#** `html` → `:host`; `body…` → `.lar-mirror…` (the container now carries `lar-mirror tc-body`).
#** A width-only <code>&#64;media</code> → <code>&#64;container</code> on the host. <code>&#64;media print</code> and every other media query keep their text.
#** The frame: `:host { container-type: inline-size; contain: layout paint; height: 80vh; min-height: 24rem; overflow: hidden }` and `.lar-mirror { height: 100%; overflow: auto }`.
#* Result: TW5's `position: fixed` lays out against the host. The story scrolls inside `.lar-mirror` while a fixed sidebar holds still. The 960px breakpoint reads the pane's width.
#* In the page (pane 758px) the sidebar now flows above the story, as TW5's narrow layout puts it. Past 960px it reads fixed inside the pane.
# ''House canon at pure local boot.'' The controller's reading of the MIRROR did not reproduce. A real dropped link sat one layer down, in the worker island.
#* Five fresh smokes from this tree (smoke1–4 at 407f3251d, smoke5 on the cure):
#** `#mirror.larMirrorReading` gave story = defaults = `lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/welcome`, palette = `…gruvbox-dark#/palette`, `tiddler-background` #282828, `page-background` #1d2021.
#** The skinny first paint shows welcome on a white frame: skinny carries no `text`, so palette colours arrive only at full.
#** The floor at seed `cc9720d2…` carries welcome (tagged Landing) and both palette slots (read straight from genesis/cas).
#** The port snapshot reads `composite.entries()`, which includes the floor face.
#* ''The dropped link:'' `floorReadFace` had no `emitInitialReplay`. The recipe replays only doc slots, so no projection ever heard the floor's rows or the oracle seed's rows. The worker island's own engine opened ''GettingStarted'': smoke4 `#projection` titles = `["GettingStarted"]`.
#* Cure: the face replays its pinned rows, first-wins, carrying `bag` = the slot. Then it replays the live seed, filtered of every title a floor row shadows. `markSyncComplete` passes through. `island-recipe` passes `bagId: slot`. One seam serves node and browser.
#* smoke5: the worker's projection titles = `["lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/welcome"]`.
#* Neither the browser recipe nor the `/genesis/cas` fetch nor the port filter dropped records. The `#/palette` title resolves as a TW5 tiddler.
#* My guess at the controller's GettingStarted screenshot, not proven: either it read the worker floor before the mirror stood, or a first snapshot that raced. Five runs showed neither.
# ''`data-lar-mirror` read null: the smoke reads too early.'' `smoke.mjs` takes `mirror` in its boot loop, which breaks at `live`, and in the projection loop, which ends once the worker's projection carries bytes. Both run before `standMirror` returns.
#* With the instrumented copy waiting for the word, every run read `full`, with `data-lar-shown="mirror"`.
#* `page-mirror.ts` still marks the host (the `mark` calls stand unchanged). Nothing needed restoring.

''Owed row closed:'' the mirror's background. `body.tc-body` → `.lar-mirror.tc-body`, so the ground reads `page-background` (#1d2021). Weld M2 styled-ground reads it.

<<~/ahu>>

