<<~ ahu slot=`#/forks-decided`>>

!! Forks decided (moʻolelo, overrulable)
* ''The sheet transform rides in the camera, not the theme.'' I rewrite the rendered sheet text rather than shadowing vanilla tiddlers. A shadow per theme would enumerate themes; the transform reads any whole-document sheet.
* ''<code>&#64;container</code> over an iframe.'' An iframe would hand TW5 a real window. It would also cost a second document and break the port's single-document camera and focus law. Container queries plus layout containment give the breakpoint and the fixed box the pane.
* ''Host height `80vh`, min 24rem.'' A fixed sidebar needs a definite height to land `bottom: 0` on, and this number fits a pane under the vessel cards. A page that wants another height overrides `#mirror { height }` from outside.
* ''The narrow pane takes TW5's own narrow layout.'' At 758px the sidebar flows above the story; that is what TW5 does under its breakpoint. Widening the panel to ≥960px would bring the fixed side-by-side layout back, unchanged.
* ''Weld M2 styled-sidebar changed meaning.'' "Computed fixed" became "inside the pane, fixed iff the pane stands at least the theme's breakpoint wide". The old reading would read red on every correct narrow pane. The breakpoint is read from the engine (vanilla's metric), never hard-coded.
* ''Floor replay origin `crdt-remote`, `edgeIsland` = the slot.'' This matches the kahua stage and the doc store's own replay. Every island now lands about 5.6k floor rows at seed, the size of the old live lares and lararium bags. If seed time grows, that cost is the floor's design showing, not a new one.

<<~/ahu>>

